WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.141 --> 00:00:01.155
- What's up, what's up world?

00:00:01.155 --> 00:00:02.108
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:02.108 --> 00:00:03.941
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:03.941 --> 00:00:05.639
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:05.639 --> 00:00:08.447
- Rawgged MC bassist for Nomadic Massive,

00:00:08.447 --> 00:00:11.797
international hip-hop band from Montreal.

00:00:11.797 --> 00:00:15.574
("Duty" by Nomadic Massive)

00:00:15.574 --> 00:00:17.648
♫ We rock the mic like all day, all night

00:00:17.648 --> 00:00:19.226
(music drowns out lyrics)

00:00:19.226 --> 00:00:20.144
♫ You know what time it is

00:00:20.144 --> 00:00:21.322
♫ We rock the mic like

00:00:21.322 --> 00:00:23.358
- Nomadic Massive started
out as a collective

00:00:23.358 --> 00:00:26.504
but morphed into a live hip-hop band.

00:00:26.504 --> 00:00:30.587
The group started officially
in 2004 in Montreal.

00:00:31.503 --> 00:00:32.336
- [Woman] There you go.

00:00:32.336 --> 00:00:33.208
- [Man] Ready?

00:00:33.208 --> 00:00:34.077
(music drowns out dialogue)

00:00:34.077 --> 00:00:35.024
One, go!

00:00:35.024 --> 00:00:38.702
("Any Sound" by Nomadic Massive)

00:00:38.702 --> 00:00:40.421
- I came here as a refugee

00:00:40.421 --> 00:00:42.668
when I was a teenager.

00:00:42.668 --> 00:00:44.241
- One of the underlying themes

00:00:44.241 --> 00:00:46.392
is the topic of identity.

00:00:46.392 --> 00:00:49.341
As immigrants, since
we express ourselves in

00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:51.240
different languages than the listener,

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.772
will then identify themselves with

00:00:52.772 --> 00:00:54.622
that little piece of Nomadic.

00:00:54.622 --> 00:00:57.356
(lively music)

00:00:57.356 --> 00:01:01.455
- How many languages are
in songs, in our band?

00:01:01.455 --> 00:01:02.958
- I'd say at least five.

00:01:02.958 --> 00:01:03.791
- Nah, I think you're wrong.

00:01:03.791 --> 00:01:04.624
- More?

00:01:04.624 --> 00:01:05.457
- French, Spanish.

00:01:05.457 --> 00:01:06.619
- [Meduza] Caribbean Patois.
- [Diegal] English, Creole.

00:01:06.619 --> 00:01:07.452
- [Diegal] Portuguese.

00:01:07.452 --> 00:01:08.311
- Arabic.

00:01:08.311 --> 00:01:09.322
And the Native languages, that's eight.

00:01:09.322 --> 00:01:11.516
- Yeah, so eight.

00:01:11.516 --> 00:01:14.770
("Any Sound" by Nomadic Massive)

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:16.740
- So a lot of times if one of us gets

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:19.772
the inspiration, and
starts a chorus in English,

00:01:19.772 --> 00:01:23.225
then one of the MCs might
really feel his story

00:01:23.225 --> 00:01:24.775
or his piece in French.

00:01:24.775 --> 00:01:26.785
And some of us just
express ourselves better

00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:29.025
in our native tongues.

00:01:29.025 --> 00:01:32.733
That combination could not have
come together anywhere else,

00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:35.578
the way it has come in Montreal.

00:01:35.578 --> 00:01:38.161
(gentle music)

00:01:39.393 --> 00:01:42.121
- Montreal is a microcosm of the world,

00:01:42.121 --> 00:01:46.288
you see different ethnic
backgrounds, and cultural groups.

00:01:48.536 --> 00:01:49.691
- People coming up to us and say

00:01:49.691 --> 00:01:51.539
"Wow, this was my favorite show because

00:01:51.539 --> 00:01:54.789
"I just felt so positive and included."

00:01:56.732 --> 00:01:58.637
This experience of
understanding multiple languages

00:01:58.637 --> 00:01:59.991
in one song, is very Montreal.

00:01:59.991 --> 00:02:02.574
(gentle music)

